status='Current Deepwell v2 candidate (2026-10-25): user called v1 "a decent first pass" but said it "needs a good bit more" and requested "300% better" across every part. This is a refinement request, not final visual acceptance or a measured percentage. music/deepwell-animation-v2/ delivers a genuine twenty-second silent 720p/30fps revision and exact three-repeat review on the same frozen planet plate (SHA-256 8c04e8fbf7af063d00cd05fb587c713f2e0a380b8274410016d072cdf9a25b9b). Water has predominantly horizontal filtered crests, weaker cross-waves, closer reflections and bounded gust/sun response. Two-depth planet-free cloud transport and a separate foreground cloud veil cross the fixed planetary body; a tight guard replaces the broad quiet halo. Far/middle/brine wisps and two terrain-guided mineral-drift paths add depth. Eight existing window groups, clearer pressure/log/level/plot activity, the existing amber service indicator, coupled lamp/spill/desk changes and restrained table/ledge daylight complete the room pass. The first v2 soft weather was too faint in assistant still review and was replaced by coherent moving forms with locally hidden resets. Source geometry/camera remain fixed; no planet remap. Full 600/1800-frame decodes/timestamps, regional/composite and quiet-neighbour seams, encoded/decoded repeat identity and twelve direct-native-to-decoded-YUV comparisons passed. Water/habitation isolated clips retained with direct controls after focused weather refinement. Every v1 manifest file remains exact. Assistant inspected source/masks/temporal/decoded stills, not continuous playback. User v2 artistic review pending; no music, opening, 4K, long assembly, new image generation, model install, commit or push. Approved original art/thumbnail and v1 preserved. See v2 README.md and validation records.'
